When updating values in the query cache which rely upon the old value, [an updater callback](https://react-query.tanstack.com/reference/QueryClient#queryclientsetquerydata) comes handy, e.g.:

```ts
setQueryData(
  ["Page.findAllBySiteId", data.siteId],
  (prev) => [...prev, data],
);
```

Instead of:

```ts
const prevPagesBySiteId =
  getQueryData(["Page.findBySiteId", data.siteId]) ?? [];
setQueryData(
  ["Page.findAllBySiteId", data.siteId],
  [...prevPagesBySiteId, data],
);
```

This overload should be made available through `trpc.useContext().setQueryData`.

